          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On September 3, 2011, around 10:50 PM, the witness observed from his balcony overlooking the Seine a formation of a dozen balls arranged in a pyramid. This formation moved silently in a trajectory opposite to usual planes descending towards ORLY. As the witness was reaching for his camcorder, part of the objects disappeared, leaving only two that quickly ascended towards a large cloud. This observation is quite typical of Thai lantern releases. The red color of the envelope, the group movement, the ascending movement and/or with the wind (light east wind that evening), the disappearance (extinction) after a few minutes, the time and date (evening of a Saturday) of the observation, are all indications supporting this hypothesis. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "379280b5827799216d8e944881e883a9deccbfc13634496aaeda51622479d071"
        }
